      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Ice-E’s Japanese text bubble closely matches what he says in English. It even emulates the \"kid’s\" apostrophe mistake in the English message by including a basic Japanese grammar mistake: using the character お (o) when を (o) should be used. With these two changes, the translator was able to keep the Japanese version of Ice-E an ice-themed mascot with an ice-themed name, saying something with bad grammar.",
